{"qid":"Q843","names":["Islamic Republic of Pakistan"],"title":"Islamic Republic of Pakistan","endonym":{"native":"Pakistan","lang":"en"},"capsule":"Pakistan was created on 14 August 1947 through the partition of British India, established as a Muslim-majority state under Governor-General Muhammad Ali Jinnah; it adopted an Islamic republic constitution in 1956. The country lost its eastern wing in 1971 when Bangladesh declared independence following a devastating civil war and Indian military intervention. Pakistan's subsequent history alternated between democratic governments and military rule under Generals Ayub Khan, Yahya Khan, Zia ul-Haq, and Pervez Musharraf, while chronic instability in the tribal northwest intensified after 2001 as a result of the Afghan war spilling across the Durand Line. By 2024 Pakistan was one of the world's five largest countries by population, possessing nuclear weapons and a disputed claim over Kashmir maintained in three wars with India.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Pakistan's international boundaries are established by the colonial-era Radcliffe Line (1947) and Durand Line; the Line of Control in Kashmir is a de facto boundary from 1972, not an international border, and the dataset geometry in that sector reflects the contested ground position rather than a legal boundary.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Pakistan","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Pakistan"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Pakistan","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pakistan"}],"britannica":"place/Pakistan","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Pakistan","rulers":[{"qid":"Q295713","name":"Liaquat Ali Khan","start":1947,"end":1951,"image":"Liaquat Ali Khan.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Liaquat%20Ali%20Khan.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Liaquat Ali Khan","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q369988","name":"Khawaja Nazimuddin","start":1951,"end":1953,"image":"Khawaja Nazimuddin.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Khawaja%20Nazimuddin.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Unknown authorUnknown author - but due to age, image in public domain","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q469875","name":"Muhammad Ali Bogra","start":1953,"end":1955,"image":"53bogra nehru (cropped).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/53bogra%20nehru%20(cropped).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Unknown authorUnknown author","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q284443","name":"Chaudhry Muhammad Ali","start":1955,"end":1956,"image":"Chaudhry Mohammad Ali.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Chaudhry%20Mohammad%20Ali.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Unknown authorUnknown author","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q155111","name":"Iskandar Ali Mirza","start":1956,"end":1958,"image":"Iskander Mirza.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Iskander%20Mirza.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Unknown authorUnknown author","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q2046354","name":"Huseyn Shaheed Suhrawardy","start":1956,"end":1957,"image":"Huseyn Shaheed Suhrawardy 1957.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Huseyn%20Shaheed%20Suhrawardy%201957.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Copyrighted free use","artist":"Unknown authorUnknown author","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q190071","name":"Ayub Khan","start":1958,"end":1969,"im